From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:06:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Stop sending unrequested Stop commands that cancel the
 client's autopilot

- ProcessState STOP: call Stop() only if the object is not already stopped.
  Stop() broadcasts CmdStop; doing it every tic stopped ships at the end of
  warp while the client was still landing ('bounce') and disabled the client's
  autopilot, and spammed every parked ship in the bubble.
- MoveToLocation: Halt() on jump arrival instead of Stop() (no CmdStop).
- Follow(): player ships that reach their follow range against a static target
  are not sent a Stop (the client holds range; Stop cancelled its autopilot).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GZgkReFMTa8JWavQEivVUA
